    "created_at": "2025-11-12T21:12:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-12T21:12:42Z",
    "body": "To be fair, dictionaries don't literally need readability of the content, just that they make the content potentially vulnerable to side-channel attacks. Something that marked the response as not needing protection from exposure through attack would also be fine.\n\nIt could be something explicit in a new header or we could decide that `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` and/or `Cache-Control: public` are enough to signal that the content doesn't need to be protected.",
